#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Shenzhen KVM for the Linux desktop: a tray icon and one window.

It talks to the shenzhen-kvm service (which runs as root) over the service's control socket:
newline-delimited JSON both ways. It subscribes to the service's state and sends the person's
choices back. It only needs python3-gi and gir1.2-gtk-3.0 (no cairo bindings: the tray glyphs
are drawn pixel by pixel).

    shenzhen-kvm-tray [--socket PATH] [--screenshot OUT.png]
"""
